# Keep the build context small and the image clean.
#
# Without this, `docker build` uploads the whole working tree to the daemon —
# including backend/venv (~281MB of a local, machine-specific virtualenv built
# for a different Python than the image) and frontend/node_modules. None of it is
# needed: the image installs dependencies from requirements.txt, and the frontend
# is deployed separately to a CDN.

# Local Python environments and caches
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# The frontend is a separate deploy target (Netlify)
frontend/

# Model files — streamed at boot, never baked into the image
*.vec
*.vec.gz
*.npy
*.pkl

# Repo/tooling noise
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
scripts/
*.md
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
